does the mailerlite api provide newsletters creations?


Context
Yes, but with limitations. Here's what the MailerLite API supports:

✅ Can do via API:

Create/update/delete campaigns (newsletters)

Set campaign name, subject, from name/email

Assign subscriber groups

Schedule or send campaigns

Fetch campaign stats (open rate, click rate, sent, unsubs)

❌ Cannot do via API:

Design the email visually (drag-and-drop editor is UI only)

Use the template builder

Preview rendered HTML in a custom UI easily

Practical reality:
The API lets you create a campaign with raw HTML content, so you could build a basic "compose newsletter" form in your admin with fields for subject, from name, HTML body, and recipient group — then send or schedule it via API.

But for anything beyond simple text/HTML emails, MailerLite's own app (app.mailerlite.com) is far better for designing newsletters.

My recommendation: Add a "Create Campaign" button in your admin MailerLite page that opens a simple form (subject, from name, select group, HTML/text body) for quick sends — and keep the "Open MailerLite" link for anything design-heavy.

